; La Aventura Original, part two: the word this port added.
;
; The same word and the same text as part one answers, and it is worth asking
; twice because the two parts number them apart: the message is 140 of one
; database and 163 of the other, and the verb is 117 against 121. A number
; copied across from the other part compiles and plays, and what it prints is
; whatever message happens to sit there — which is to say the test that catches
; it is this one, in the part that was not the model.
;
; See part1-qdaad.qtest for what the EXPECTs are walking.
;
;   qdaad compile -i examples/AO/ZXSpectrum/+3/part2/game.sce -m pc -s vga -f ddb -o tmp/AO2 --part 2
;   qrun -i tmp/AO2.ddb -T examples/AO/test/part2-qdaad.qtest

TEST "La Aventura Original, parte II: la palabra QDAAD"

SEED 1989
TIMEOUT 1

STEP "Clave de acceso"
  EXPECT "¿Clave de acceso?"
  INPUT "TIMACUS"
END

STEP "Arranque de la segunda parte"
  EXPECT "Con un click la puerta se cierra mágicamente..."
  KEY ENTER
  EXPECT "Los rayos del sol iluminan la caverna"
END

STEP "QDAAD responde con el aviso del compilador"
  INPUT  QDAAD
  EXPECT "Queru's DAAD Compiler"
  EXPECT "Jorge Fuertes AKA Queru"
  EXPECT "descompilación, compilación y empaquetado de QDAAD"
  EXPECT "software libre en 2026 y disponible en Github."
  EXPECT "¡Gracias por jugar!"
END

STEP "Y AD sigue dando los créditos de 1989"
  INPUT  AD
  EXPECT "Tambien participaron"
END
